Package: com.qingc12.pullovermf
Name: PullOverMF
Version: 0.1.3
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: MultiFloat personal fork of PullOver X (GPL-3.0). Floating multitask window / split view for iOS 14+ (roothide / arm64e). 0.1.3: (1) CRITICAL FIX - 0.1.2 crashed inside the dylib constructor (it called NSDateFormatter / [UIDevice currentDevice] before Foundation/UIKit were ready in SpringBoard), so the whole tweak failed to load and even the handle disappeared; logging is now split into a pure-C MFLogRawC() for the constructor phase and MFLog() for normal runtime; (2) new STHENO-STYLE RING PICKER: a semicircular dial pinned to the screen edge with app icons arranged along the arc (modelled on Stheno's RingView/RingType - 'half disc / right-angle disc / disc' - with IconWidth / Radius / HeightFraction / RotationAngle parameters found in its binaries), tapping an icon pins that app and opens the float, long-pressing an icon removes it from the dial (persisted to ringApps); (3) the dial is summoned by an edge gesture - a transparent trigger strip on a configurable screen edge that responds to a swipe (18pt in any direction) or a tap, matching Stheno's 'EdgeBar / trigger edge' approach while staying hook-free; (4) every step is logged to /var/mobile/PullOverMF.log so the next round can verify whether the edge strip still receives touches above a full-screen app before any SpringBoard gesture hook is added.
Maintainer: QingC12
Author: PullOver X by mlgm / PullOver Pro by c1d3rDev / fork by QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 14.0)
Priority: optional
